# 📘 Calculative Foundation

## 🌟 Project Overview

The **Calculative Foundation** project demonstrates the application of fundamental mathematical and statistical concepts using Python and Jupyter Notebook. The project covers data analysis, matrix operations, probability calculations, covariance analysis, eigenvalue decomposition, LU decomposition, and Singular Value Decomposition (SVD).

---

## 🎯 Objectives

✅ Understand basic statistical concepts

✅ Perform matrix operations and transformations

✅ Analyze covariance and correlation between variables

✅ Compute eigenvalues and eigenvectors of covariance matrices

✅ Perform LU Decomposition

✅ Apply Singular Value Decomposition (SVD)

✅ Understand dimensionality reduction techniques

---

## 🛠️ Tools & Technologies

| Tool                | Purpose                    |
| ------------------- | -------------------------- |
| 🐍 Python           | Programming Language       |
| 📓 Jupyter Notebook | Development Environment    |
| 🔢 NumPy            | Numerical Computing        |
| 🐼 Pandas           | Data Manipulation          |
| 📊 Matplotlib       | Data Visualization         |
| ⚙️ SciPy            | Scientific Computing       |
| 🤖 Scikit-learn     | Machine Learning Utilities |

---

## 📂 Project Structure

### 📖 Part A – Theory

* 📚 Introduction to Calculative Foundations
* 🔢 Matrix Fundamentals
* 🎲 Probability Concepts
* 📈 Statistical Measures
* 🧮 Linear Algebra Basics

### 💻 Part B – Practical Implementation

* 📥 Data Loading and Exploration
* 🧹 Data Preprocessing
* 📊 Descriptive Statistics
* 🔄 Matrix Operations
* 📉 Data Visualization using Matplotlib

### 📈 Part C – Statistical Analysis

* 📌 Mean, Median, Mode
* 📌 Variance and Standard Deviation
* 📌 Correlation Analysis
* 📌 Covariance Matrix Generation

### 🔬 Part D – Eigenvalues & Matrix Decomposition

1️⃣ Compute Covariance Matrix

2️⃣ Calculate Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors

3️⃣ Perform LU Decomposition

4️⃣ Perform Singular Value Decomposition (SVD)

5️⃣ Analyze Variance Explained

6️⃣ Study Dimensionality Reduction Concepts

